given some random data in array but you need to convert it into heap 



<!-- approach  -->

start with nonleaf node 

now the basic idea is to create heap of every part and we know that leaf nodes are already heap so we skip that and continue from nonLeaf nodes 

run loop from that nonLeaf till root node i.e 0,1 indexed, based on indexing given 


now find the index with the largest / smallest based on min/max heap you need to create 

once you got the index then swap with current index 

then call the recursion for swapped node as we just need to check that below subtree is also a heap





tc- n (this is logical beacause you are running loop from nonLeaf to root and for every node you are doing heapify which costs logn

but also it doesn't count as nlogn but n only)

Nodes near the root cost more, but there are very few of them. Nodes near the leaves are numerous, but cost almost nothing to heapify. That's why building a heap takes (O(N)) time.




sc - logn (sc is justified because we are running recursion data and heap is also a cbt so it can be max logn and not n for skewed tree)